WEBVTT

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.480
Well.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.450
Good morning, Kazumi.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.490
Damn it!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.530
Get your damned dirty paws off my Mi-chan!

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.850
That's enough, Sis...

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.100
Damn that Kasumi! Was she trying to kill me?

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.750
\h\hObi Sash Tsukumogami
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKirio\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.750
\h\h\h\h\hMalison Exorcist\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h\h\hKagami Kazumi

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.750
She wouldn't if you'd just behave.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.070
'Sup?

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.260
\h\hShiramine Shitone\h\h

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.260
\h\h\h\h\hOsanai Osane\h\h\h\h\h

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.260
\h\hChikaishi Chikao\h\h

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.470
Good morning, Kagami.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.260
Good morning.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.150
Something feels... off.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.260
You think so, too?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.770
What? Did you forget to put these on?

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.760
What do you think you're doing?!

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.260
You wanted to see as badly as I did!

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.830
Same old same old.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.530
Yes. It seems that way.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.820
Wait.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.630
Everyone, try to remember...

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.930
exactly where we are.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.950
This is a dream

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.020
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.090
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.510
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.510
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.510
<b>Chapter 4</b>

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.510
<b>Swapped!</b>

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:35.900
"Swapped!"

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.930
\h\hSome Days Earlier\h\h

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.930
\h\hSome Days Earlier\h\h

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:38.750
Satou-san?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.650
Here.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.790
Takayama-kun?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.450
Takayama-kun?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.180
Attendance

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.060
A lot of people absent today...

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.060
Sensei, we can't have class like this!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.450
He's right. We should have 
a study period instead.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.160
I'm going to consult with the other teachers.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.320
Study quietly until I get back, okay?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.690
Yeah!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:03.900
Hey, wanna do versus mode?

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.120
I'm starving, dude.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.580
Eat your lunch, then!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.150
Keep it down, okay?

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.190
Sure!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:13.350
Hey.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.430
You hear about how Takayama's been absent

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.530
because of some kinda sleeping sickness?

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:19.780
A sleeping sickness?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.090
He won't wake up, no matter what they try.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.420
The doctors have even thrown in the towel.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.100
Kiriha-san?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.890
Indeed. This calls for the 
Troubleshooters' Office.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.600
Troubleshooters'
Office

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.490
The sleeping sickness that has been 
spreading among the second-years

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:37.880
Today's Subject:
The Sleeping Sickness
 -More students have
started missing classes
over the last few days
 -Seems to be spreading among
second-years
 -Once asleep, they don't wake up

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.130
started a few days ago,

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Takayama Takashi</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Sick          Sick       Sick         Sick</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Chikaishi Chisato</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Nazuki Natsuki</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Sick          Sick       Sick         Sick</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Mikawa Mitsuo</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Sick          Sick       Sick         Sick</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Misa Misako</b>

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.860
<b>Sick          Sick</b>

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.860
and at this point, 
has affected about half of them.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.900
Even in the other classes?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.990
There's no doubt this is an amasogi's doing.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.930
We'd better solve it fast, then.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.780
Right. And on that note...

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.310
I've arranged for an advisor 
to help this club of ours

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.880
deal with these ever-increasing 
cases of aberrations.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.040
Is it a woman?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:00.670
Yes.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.990
Is she young?

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:02.980
She looks that way, yes.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.140
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPillowy\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.140
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPillowy\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.140
Is she... pillowy?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.070
No.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.760
I'm your advisor, Shirayama Kukuri.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.760
Shirayama Kukuri-sensei

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.890
Yes!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:14.400
<b>Advisor</b>

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.340
A regional goddess... as an advisor?

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.400
Anything goes, huh?

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.900
Fashion Glasses

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.900
That bein' the case,

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.400
\h\h\h\hThe room of the first victim,\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h\h\h\hTakayama Takashi\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.400
\h\h\h\hThe room of the first victim,\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h\h\h\hTakayama Takashi\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.660
you can leave this whole mess to me.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:26.410
If an aberration's behind it all, 
we check the first student who got sick.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:35.170
\h\hMother's Testimony\h\h

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:35.170
\h\hMother's Testimony\h\h

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:31.260
According to his mother, she thought 
he'd left for school as usual,

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:32.860
but when she got home from work,

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.170
he was still asleep in his room.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.420
I've seen a ruckus caused by 
a tsukumogami pillow before.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:44.930
The wielder at the time ended up 
draggin' other folks into his dream.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.380
That does sound similar 
to this sleeping sickness.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.140
Yep.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.620
Which is why I figure this here 
pillow oughta be our amasogi!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.440
Huh?

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.690
We checked the first three students 
who fell to the sleeping sickness,

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Mikawa Mitsuo</b>

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Takayama Takashi</b>

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Nazuki Natsuki</b>

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.990
but there was no sign of the amasogi.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.570
I see...

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.570
This is what you "figured"?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.060
Because you were completely off.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.330
I mean, it seemed real sketchy...

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:15.370
The reasoning of looking into the 
first victims made sense, but...

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.710
Those guys, huh?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.710
<b>Mikawa Mitsuo</b>

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.710
<b>Takayama Takashi</b>

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.710
<b>Nazuki Natsuki</b>

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.150
They always were hanging 
out, come to think of it.

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.310
No telling what kind of 
trouble they got up to.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.290
Man, that's nasty!

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.970
I don't get you!

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.970
Come on, it's time for class.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.340
Is there some clue about 
the three of them?

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.480
<b>Attendance</b>

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.580
Wait a minute...

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.070
Sensei!

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.270
What's wrong?

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.980
The attendance sheet.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.290
The first day he was absent,

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.660
Takayama's mother didn't 
know he was still asleep.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.280
<b>Shiramine Shirou</b>

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.280
<b>Takayama Takashi</b>

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.280
<b>Chikaishi Chisato</b>

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.280
<b>Nazuki Natsuki</b>

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.760
But you marked Takayama 
and his friends as "sick,"

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.750
without even checking with their parents!

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.990
Which means... you must have known 
why they were absent from the start.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.250
I...

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.760
Sensei, we know all about 
these kinds of incidents!

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.370
You have to tell us what's 
going on so we can help you!

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.790
Sensei!

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.050
Sorry for barging in like this.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.160
It seems this pillow is the amasogi.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:37.910
Then after she wakes up, 
we need to ask her to destroy it.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:42.010
Nah. She fled into her dreams.

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:44.920
Isuzu ain't gonna wake up on her own.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.630
What if we destroy the pillow?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.900
All the folks inside her dream 
are gonna end up stuck there.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.800
What do we do, then?

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.110
This is the kinda thing you 
need Shirayama-sensei for!

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:03.940
Hey there. I'm the dreaming 
pillow tsugumomo, Bakura.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.940
Dreaming Pillow Tsugumomo\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hBakura\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:08.940
Bakura-chan's got the power to 
get people in and outta dreams!

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.950
I see. The idea is to try to convince 
Isuzu within her dream, then?

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:19.080
That would be ideal, since it 
would avoid malison atonement.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.660
If you're unable to convince her,

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:27.850
the same pillow amasogi should 
exist in her dream realm,

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.580
and you'll need to destroy that.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.970
So either convince her... or destroy 
the pillow inside her dream?

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:42.730
The dream realm is distinct from reality, 
but connected by your mind.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:51.490
So if you're hurt inside the dream, 
it will have an affect on your body.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:58.870
Therefore, to minimize the danger, 
we'll be splitting your minds up,

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:03.750
and your other half will be the one 
that enters the dream realm.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.630
Other half?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.890
On your initial entry into the dream,

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:14.890
you may be confused 
and not realize it's a dream.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:20.080
In that case, maybe we could agree on a 
keyword I can write in my sketchbook?

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.640
Once we see that, it should 
help us realize the truth.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.210
Tadataka, be ready in case things go awry.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:27.400
Leave it to me.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.400
Here we go, then.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.880
People and dreams,

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:39.590
connected in a fleeting moment, 
in which all can be as they truly wish...

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:46.490
That's right! We're inside Iraha-sensei's dream!

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:50.920
In reality, I'm a boy, and Kirio-kun is a girl!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.050
And our goal here is to 
talk sense into Isuzu!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.620
I didn't realize this is what 
she meant by our "other half"!

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.140
It's kind of awkward to run!

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.500
I didn't realize these got in the way so much...

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.610
Iraha-sensei!

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.210
What's wrong? You shouldn't 
be running in the hallway.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.440
We've come to bring you back.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.490
Release the students from this dream!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.450
Or else we'll be forced to destroy 
that pillow of yours.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.790
An amasogi capable of something on this scale

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.810
is going to result in a fierce atonement!

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.700
Sensei, please!

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:29.350
You actually made your 
way into this dream, huh?

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.960
You two live up to your reputation.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:33.210
What?

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.490
I knew you'd try to destroy the pillow, too.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:40.000
I'm thinking your friends are waiting nearby,

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.770
waiting to destroy the pillow 
you stole from my room

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.480
inside the dream when you 
give them the signal, right?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:49.860
Such a shame, though. That one's a decoy.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.490
How did you know all this?

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:59.900
I can't let anyone interrupt this dream.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:03.140
It's time for your shadows 
to consume you, too.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:20.020
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:20.020
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.500
Tsugu Tsugumomo!

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:24.520
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:24.520
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.510
Tsugu Tsugumomo!

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.140
Who are they?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.540
Is that us?!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.160
They can use obis, too?!

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.790
This must be what Bakura-san warned us about!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.090
There's one other thing to warn you about.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:56.550
Inside the dream, there's a 
chance your shadow selves,

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:00.800
the portion of yourselves that you normally 
suppress, might come to the surface.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.950
If you encounter your shadow in the dream...

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.560
What'll happen?

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:11.310
It'll attack you and try to take your place.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.330
Sledgehammer Weave!

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.570
<i>I suppose anyone would be evenly
 matched with their own shadow.</i>

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.820
Kagami!

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.580
Are these...

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.550
The shadows of the other 
students, most likely.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:32.330
That's right. And they're 
all so well-behaved.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:36.510
You know, people grow a lot by 
grappling with their shadows.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:44.340
If all of you can accept your shadows, 
I'll release the others from this dream.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:49.200
That way, everyone at school 
will be more obedient.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.980
That's a win for everyone, isn't it?

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:55.850
It isn't! You're just trying to control 
your students by forcing them to obey!

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:57.980
We can't do as you ask.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.990
Fair enough. In that case...

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.740
I'll have to educate you, too!

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:11.690
They escaped...

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.590
<i>What is this? How are we being forced back?!</i>

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.880
I thought we were supposed 
to be evenly matched!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.390
Even? What're you talking about?

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:32.390
The two of you can only generate 
three obis, including the original.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.550
But us?

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.540
We can tap into all our latent strength,

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.150
with none of the subconscious restraint.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.850
Eight obis?!

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.410
We have to fight back somehow!

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:56.210
Hey, Kazumi!

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:07.180
From now on, you will be 
controlled by your own shadow.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.650
Get your hands off my girl!

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.690
Impregnable Fortress

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.850
That was the shadow of Iraha Isuzu.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:28.610
She's trying to make everyone subservient 
by dragging them into this dream.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.220
You're...

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.200
I'm the real Iraha Isuzu.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.420
Huh?!

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.600
But... you look...

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.560
Well, we're inside a dream.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.090
Apparently, it's possible 
to change how you look.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:50.660
If you really are Iraha-sensei, 
can you explain how this happened?

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:55.900
My students didn't take me seriously.

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:58.350
That's why they'd never listen to me,

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.160
and I could never bring 
any order to my classes.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.360
Everyone! Quiet down!

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.820
That's what I was worrying about 
when I stumbled upon that pillow.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:13.620
<b>No talking!!</b>

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:13.220
Inside my dreams, I could 
do exactly what I wanted.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:17.620
<b>Please be quiet</b>

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:17.620
But in reality, I was the same as usual...

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.930
And before I realized what was going on,

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:24.460
I ended up dragging many 
students into my dream.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:29.130
I think that's what my 
shadow wanted all along.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:34.970
I managed to escape from her, and I've been 
hiding from her by staying in this form.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:42.270
To resolve this, we need to get 
our hands on the amasogi pillow...

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:46.280
I'm pretty sure the shadow Isuzu has it.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.850
We need to think of a way to steal it.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:53.620
But how? Kazumi's busy, 
and if it's only us...

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:01.540
I have an idea.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:08.670
This is where you've been hiding?

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.430
Are you finally done playing hide-and-seek?

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:17.330
I was wrong to hope that my dreams 
could help me change for the better.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.210
Now, give my students back!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.190
<i>A pointer?!</i>

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:27.970
<i>How could she do that with a pointer?!</i>

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.440
Split Down the Center

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:30.970
Raging Inferno Surges Forth

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:41.090
<i>There it is! She was hiding it inside her body?</i>

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.420
<i>Now, if I can just destroy it...</i>

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:53.340
Burst of Strange Strength

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.170
Oh, I see. You used yojijukugo idioms.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.340
How fitting for a Japanese language teacher.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:57.350
A power born from the dream...

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.350
But unfortunately for you, 
this is a nightmare.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:10.420
And if you can use this power, 
then, as your shadow, so can I.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.190
Burst of Strange Strength

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.360
Transforming of an Apparition

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.130
<i>I can't gather my strength...</i>

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.380
Don't waste your time resisting.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:29.380
I'm you.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.850
And you can't surpass yourself.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:36.660
<i>Surpass myself?</i>

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.670
Kirio-kun!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.140
Right you are.

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:50.400
What a waste of time.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:54.400
But... the end result is going to be same!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:58.750
<i>If this shadow is using all of my skills...</i>

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.160
<i>Then I just have to go past that!</i>

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.830
Take this!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.670
<i>Faster than yesterday... 
Stronger than yesterday...</i>

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.390
<i>The same way...</i>

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:11.420
I always do!

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.180
<b>Spiral Weave: Eightfold Edges</b>

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:15.180
Spiral Weave: Eightfold Edges!

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:21.430
<i>She was able to use eight, too?! 
And that shape...</i>

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:25.630
<i>Did she use a weave I don't 
know at the last second?!</i>

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:27.280
Go, Kazumi!

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.690
Spiral Weave:

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.190
<b>Spiral Weave: Flowering Eight Folds!</b>

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:32.190
Flowering Eight Folds!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.510
Impossible!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.200
A spider...

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.460
Help!

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:52.430
Wh-What are those things?

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.170
My sketchbook creations.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.260
And my popularity fragrance!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.330
I'll keep the students out of your hair!

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.810
How can ordinary students 
like you do this?!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.690
These powers come from the 
amasogis we were involved with.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:14.180
We got the idea from how Sensei 
was able to change her appearance.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:18.270
We'll hold her down. Use that 
opportunity to get the pillow, Sensei!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.200
You pests!

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.710
Hang on! I'll get you free!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.350
Sledgehammer Weave!

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.370
You're late, Kagami!

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.480
Sorry!

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:49.540
I had to help Shitone preserve 
her virtue on the way here!

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.230
Crap! It works too well!

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:55.980
Kagami! The pillow is inside her!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.740
Remember to have Isuzu finish it!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.930
Got it!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:02.120
Sensei!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.740
Roger that!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:09.750
One Shot, One Kill!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.000
<b>One Shot, One Kill</b>

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.520
Thank you. You all saved me.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.330
All's well that ends well.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.700
Your willpower is what won in the end.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:35.270
Besides, we couldn't do much on our own...

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:39.650
All those acrobatics must've torn it open.

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:43.770
Eek!

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:46.550
No worries. I can cover you up.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.970
Hey! What're you doing?!

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:53.410
Hey! Good work, everyone.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:54.170
Bakura-san!

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:57.600
Right. The amasogi's creator 
destroyed it herself.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.760
That's a relief.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:03.180
I'll be waiting for you all to return.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.810
Wait, how do we get back?

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:08.490
You're inside a dream.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:14.980
So if you go to sleep here, 
you'll wake up in reality.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:19.380
I suppose we'll all head 
home and go to bed, then.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:21.190
Kind of an anticlimax, huh?

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:25.740
All right, off we go, Kazumi. Homeward bound.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.950
I've got a really bad feeling about this.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.030
It's going to be a long night...

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.860
See you soon.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.350
Hey! What are you planning to do to Kagami?!

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:35.850
Hey, no inappropriate relations!

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.460
\h\hThe Next Day\h\h

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.460
\h\hThe Next Day\h\h

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:41.210
Excuse me, Takayama-kun! 
Where is your homework?

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:44.380
Sensei seems to be feeling a lot better.

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:42.620
Huh?

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:44.380
Don't "huh" me!

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:46.970
That's what she's really like.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.970
She's been repressing herself up until now.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.560
Think about what you did!

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.970
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:56.020
You're free to unleash all your pent-up 
aggression on me, if you like.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:21:00.230
You're the one who just unleashed on me.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:02.420
And after I told you it hurt...

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.820
I was, er, caught up in the moment... 
you know, having trouble holding back...

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.660
Obina-san! You're not 
supposed to make them cry!

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:09.990
Sorry...

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:44.620
You can do whatever you want, Shirou-kun.

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:48.420
No good!

00:22:48.770 --> 00:22:50.690
I'm not getting turned on at all!

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:54.350
It's only natural. Right now, we're women.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:57.890
It stands to reason we'd be attracted to men.

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:59.560
Wait, hang on a second...

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:01.450
Maybe...

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:04.610
I'm just not turned on 
from looking at myself!

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:05.930
Please settle down.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.450
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hVisual Metaphor\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.450
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hVisual Metaphor\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:16.680
I feel like I've gained a new perspective.

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:18.910
You owe me big for this!

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:33.010
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:23.190
Kotetsu-kun is unconscious 
and won't wake up.

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:24.750
Sunao-san is worried about him,

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.290
so we accompany her to a mysterious 
altar in the mountains.

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:29.720
Will the two of them be reunited?

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:33.010
Next time on <i>Tsugu Tsugumomo</i>, 
Chapter 5: "Sunao and Kotetsu."

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:33.010
<b>Sunao and Kotetsu</b>

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:34.300
Don't miss it!

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Don't miss it!</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Illustration by: KAKERU</b>
